}

docs {
  # Profile Links
  
  Profile links allow you to add custom social media and professional links to your profile beyond the core URLs (LinkedIn, GitHub, Portfolio).
  
  ## Overview
  
  Profile links are stored separately from the main profile and can be:
  - **Public** (`is_public: true`) - Visible to everyone viewing your profile
  - **Private** (`is_public: false`) - Only visible to you
  
  Links can be associated with predefined platforms (like Twitter, Instagram, etc.) or be custom links.
  
  ## Getting Profile Links
  
  To retrieve your profile with links included, use the `include_links` query parameter:
  
  ```
  GET /api/v1/profiles/me?include_links=true
  GET /api/v1/profiles/:identifier?include_links=true
  ```
  
  ### Response Example
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Profile retrieved successfully",
    "data": {
      "id": "uuid-here",
      "username": "johndoe",
      "bio": "Full-stack developer...",
      "profile_links": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "profile_id": "uuid-here",
          "platform_id": 2,
          "url": "https://twitter.com/johndoe",
          "category": "social",
          "is_public": true,
          "sort_order": 0,
          "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
          "link_platforms": {
            "id": 2,
            "name": "twitter",
            "display_name": "Twitter",
            "category": "social",
            "icon": "twitter"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "profile_id": "uuid-here",
          "platform_id": null,
          "url": "https://myblog.dev",
          "category": "personal",
          "is_public": true,
          "sort_order": 1,
          "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:35:00Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-15T10:35:00Z",
          "link_platforms": null
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Profile Link Structure
  
  | Field | Type | Description |
  |-------|------|-------------|
  | `id` | number | Unique link ID |
  | `profile_id` | string (UUID) | Profile owner ID |
  | `platform_id` | number \| null | Optional reference to predefined platform |
  | `url` | string | The link URL (required, must be valid URL) |
  | `category` | string \| null | Link category (e.g., "social", "professional", "personal") |
  | `is_public` | boolean | Whether link is visible publicly (default: `true`) |
  | `sort_order` | number | Display order (0 = first, default: `0`) |
  | `created_at` | string | Creation timestamp |
  | `updated_at` | string | Last update timestamp |
  | `link_platforms` | object \| null | Platform metadata if `platform_id` is set |
  
  ## Link Categories
  
  Common categories for organizing links:
  - `social` - Social media profiles
  - `professional` - Professional networks and platforms
  - `personal` - Personal websites and blogs
  - `portfolio` - Portfolio and showcase sites
  - `community` - Community platforms and forums
  - `other` - Other types of links
  
  ## Public vs Private Links
  
  - **Public links** (`is_public: true`) are visible to anyone viewing your profile
  - **Private links** (`is_public: false`) are only visible to you when authenticated
  
  When viewing someone else's profile, only their public links are returned.
  
  ## Platform Integration
  
  Links can be associated with predefined platforms in the system. Platforms provide:
  - Display name
  - Icon/logo
  - Category
  - URL validation patterns
  
  If `platform_id` is `null`, the link is a custom link without platform association.
  
  ## Example Use Cases
  
  ### Social Media Links
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://twitter.com/username",
    "category": "social",
    "is_public": true,
    "sort_order": 0
  }
  ```
  
  ### Personal Blog
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://myblog.dev",
    "category": "personal",
    "is_public": true,
    "sort_order": 1
  }
  ```
  
  ### Private Portfolio
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://private-portfolio.com",
    "category": "portfolio",
    "is_public": false,
    "sort_order": 2
  }
  ```
  
  ### Professional Platform
  ```json
  {
    "platform_id": 5,
    "url": "https://dribbble.com/username",
    "category": "professional",
    "is_public": true,
    "sort_order": 0
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - Profile links are separate from core profile URLs (`linkedin_url`, `github_url`, `portfolio_url`)
  - Links are returned in `sort_order` order (ascending)
  - Only public links are included when viewing other users' profiles
  - URL validation ensures all links are properly formatted
  - Custom links (without `platform_id`) are fully supported
  
  ## Future Endpoints
  
  Dedicated CRUD endpoints for profile links may be available:
  - `POST /api/v1/profiles/me/links` - Create a new link
  - `PUT /api/v1/profiles/me/links/:id` - Update a link
  - `DELETE /api/v1/profiles/me/links/:id` - Delete a link
  - `GET /api/v1/profiles/me/links` - List all your links
  
  Check the API documentation for the latest endpoint availability.
}

